{
  "dom_id": "step-e3666",
  "name": "Example: Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions",
  "problem": "Express $\\cos^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)} - \\sin^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{24})-{sin}^{2}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{24}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{24}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
